From: Local M2 diagnostics
Subject: [PATCH] Correct wait-stop handling and capture init child exit/proc state

Reason: probe10 passed stop-marker127 as a signal and ignored PTRACE_CONT
errno5. Policy compilation passes on recovery and DS-ACK; a correct recorder
is needed before attributing the bootloop to SELinux. Add SIGCHLD siginfo so
compiler completion is observable, and mount private procfs for snapshots.
Files: diagnostics/bootlogger_pid1_probe11.c (derived from retained probe10).
Verification: AArch64 static build; signal-forward, ptrace attach, exec-error,
private proc and cold namespace tests PASS on TWRP4.9.118 and DS-ACK4.9.337;
parent PID1 mountinfo hashes unchanged. BOOT image audit preserves kernel,
DTB and cmdline, original init as init.real, and every other CPIO entry.
PID1 boot runtime remains pending at preparation time. No normal fork changes.

